# Site resources

Maintainer notes live in `docs/resources.md`. Never copy them into `content/`, `static/`, a Hugo page, or a commit message that restates secrets. Hugo publishes `content/` and `static/` only.

- Cursor: `[params.cursor]` in `hugo.toml` and `static/images/cursor.png` (32×32). `x` and `y` are the hotspot. Delete `image` to use the normal pointer.
- Banner: `[params.home]` `bannerDir` (folder under `static/`; Hugo shuffles and preloads one per render), fallback `banner`, plus `bannerAlt`. Markup is `layouts/index.html`; `home.js` only decode-reveals. Homepage title under the banner: `displayTitle`, `titleFont`, optional `titleFontUrl`. `static/css/retro.css` adds twinkling corner sparkles on the homepage banner only — not gallery, article, or writing-index thumbs (no border/wash; GeoCities vibe, not CRT). Fun custom cursor is owner-later — leave `[params.cursor]` alone unless asked.
- Sprites: `[[params.sprites]]` in `hugo.toml` + strips in `static/images/sprites/`. Source sheets live in `assets-src/sprites/` (not published). Shortcode `sprite`. `[params.home] logoSprite` makes that strip the home nav button (`layouts/partials/header.html`). Misdreavus is front-hover only; Kagura rows are `kagura-walk` / `kagura-down` / `kagura-attack` (wind is baked into the attack frames); Sango is `sango-idle` / `sango-attack` / `sango-boomerang` (separate spinning Hiraikotsu projectile); SkiFree yeti is the subscribe footer. Homepage dock: Sango left of the ticker (idle while Kagura’s wind sweep passes; click → throw boomerang at Kagura, she goes down, boomerang returns, both recover), Kagura parks right after the slash. Re-slice with `scripts/slice-*.mjs`.
- Player: `layouts/partials/player.html`, `static/js/player.js`, `static/css/player.css`. One HTML-audio chrome on every page: desktop footer stack with Grundo centered above the stop button and ↑ halfway between the skip button and the window edge; mobile is the same bar without Grundo, parked on the same footer line. The counter or yeti, the player, and the reserved ↑ slot share one gap and the group is centered in the footer. One shared row on every page (`site-shell.css` + `placeFooterRow()`), so phone footers look identical; the yeti is native size on phones. Phone nav: Misdreavus | centered links | Pancham. Homepage dock is Sango, the ticker, and Kagura on desktop; below 45rem the pets are hidden. The ↑ stays on every page. Every page shares `.site-shell` (`assets/css/layout.css`): `--middle-column`, `--aside-width`, `--aside-gap`. Music keeps playing only when the layout wraps the page in `#page-root` and includes the player partial after it.
- Playlist: `static/audio/playlist.json` is the local test list (`title`, `src`). The fetch URL is in `static/js/player.js`. A remote folder works only as HTTP URLs plus that JSON file and CORS. Do not call a Plex or Symphony library, a drive path, or put an API token in the site.
- Socials: `[[params.socialLinks]]` in `hugo.toml` (right nav). Per-page buttons: front matter `buttons`, the `button` shortcode, or `kind = "button"` in `[params.home.footer]`.
- Backdrop: `[params.backdrop.bottom-right]`, `bottom-left`, `top-right`, and `top-left`, each with a file under `static/images/`. Corner art is homepage-only (fixed); bottom-right image is reserved for read-me `.sword-figure` (`sword_figure = true`) and is not emitted as a fixed corner. Max size is that corner's `maxwidth` and `maxheight`; a smaller file is not scaled up. `image = ""` leaves that corner empty.
